  "stem": "For the linear function \\(f\\), \\(f(2) = 7\\) and \\(f(10) = -5\\). For what value of \\(x\\) is \\(f(x) = 2x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "20/7"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Slope: \\(\\frac{-5 - 7}{10 - 2} = -\\frac{3}{2}\\), so \\(f(x) = 7 - \\frac{3}{2}(x - 2) = -\\frac{3}{2}x + 10\\).",
    "Set \\(-\\frac{3}{2}x + 10 = 2x\\): \\(\\frac{7}{2}x = 10\\), so \\(x = \\frac{20}{7}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nm = Rational(-5 - 7, 10 - 2)\nf = 7 + m*(x - 2)\nsol = solve(Eq(f, 2*x), x)\nassert sol == [Rational(20, 7)]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
